        }
      ],
      "id": "jsaipka"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6gk6q31",
      "content": "Biochemistry is the study of chemical substances and vital processes occurring in living organisms. In nursing competitive examinations such as RRB Nursing, questions are commonly asked from biomolecules, enzymes, vitamins, minerals, metabolism, and acid–base balance. Understanding biochemical processes helps nurses understand disease mechanisms, drug actions, and nutritional deficiencies."
    },
    {
      "id": "qix6yiw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Biomolecules"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jb4qpnk",
      "content": "Biomolecules are organic molecules present in living organisms that are essential for structure and metabolism. The major biomolecules include carbohydrates, proteins, lipids, and nucleic acids."
    },
    {
      "id": "xuhafvy",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
