          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Biomolecule</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Main Function</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Carbohydrates</p>",
            "<p>Primary source of energy</p>",
            "<p>Glucose, starch, glycogen</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Proteins</p>",
            "<p>Structural components and enzymes</p>",
            "<p>Hemoglobin, enzymes</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lipids</p>",
            "<p>Energy storage and cell membranes</p>",
            "<p>Fats, phospholipids, cholesterol</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nucleic Acids</p>",
            "<p>Genetic information storage</p>",
            "<p>DNA, RNA</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rw09qhx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Carbohydrate Metabolism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "akq70o7",
      "content": "Carbohydrates are the body's major energy source. Glucose metabolism occurs mainly through glycolysis, the Krebs cycle, and oxidative phosphorylation."
    },
    {
      "id": "l4vq814",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Process</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Glycolysis</p>",
            "<p>Breakdown of glucose to pyruvate producing ATP</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Krebs Cycle</p>",
            "<p>Occurs in mitochondria producing energy carriers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Oxidative Phosphorylation</p>",
            "<p>Electron transport chain producing ATP</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Glycogenesis</p>",
            "<p>Formation of glycogen from glucose</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Glycogenolysis</p>",
            "<p>Breakdown of glycogen into glucose</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lojfzrf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Protein Metabolism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8w9qzlm",
      "content": "Proteins are composed of amino acids and are essential for tissue repair, enzyme formation, hormone production, and immune function."
    },
