        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Digestion</p>",
            "<p>Proteins are broken down into amino acids in stomach and intestine</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Transamination</p>",
            "<p>Transfer of amino group between amino acids</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Deamination</p>",
            "<p>Removal of amino group producing ammonia</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Urea Cycle</p>",
            "<p>Conversion of ammonia to urea in liver</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "k6ovdkb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Lipid Metabolism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j6wpeug",
      "content": "Lipids provide long‑term energy storage and are important components of cell membranes."
