    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Glycolysis takes place in the cytoplasm and produces a net yield of 2 ATP and 2 NADH molecules per glucose molecule.",
        "The urea cycle occurs predominantly in the liver to convert toxic ammonia into urea for excretion.",
        "Fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K) can accumulate in the body leading to toxicity, whereas water-soluble vitamins (B, C) are readily excreted.",
        "Metabolic acidosis occurs when blood pH falls below 7.35 due to bicarbonate loss or acid accumulation."
      ],
      "id": "ix55wqj"
    },
    {
